  "rulings": [
    {
      "topic": "364 why",
      "selection": "Keep E w4 CI'I PHYIR/why d5.",
      "reason": "The full expression has glossary why and functions as an interrogative lexical unit here. Its internal genitive and PHYIR remain intact; a lexical multi-syllable interrogative need not be relabeled as a flat particle."
    },
    {
      "topic": "364/366 asking",
      "selection": "Keep E ZHE NA/ask d3 in both rows.",
      "reason": "The local construction introduces an asking event. One may is supplied impersonal framing; retaining ask preserves the secure contribution. Whole GANG ZHE NA has broader one may ask/how glossary evidence, but that does not prove the isolated ZHE NA owns all of that wording. The unrelated mined correct perception is not adopted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "364 genitives",
      "selection": "Add T p3 KYI/with as final p30 and T p6 GI/with as final p31.",
      "reason": "Each complete case particle links a counted group to its domain, expressed locally as involved with thought and involved with body and speech. With is the secure relation. GI literally also attests involved with; keep this broader counterevidence while leaving involved outside the tighter span. These are independent syllables, not separated suffixes."
    },
    {
      "topic": "364 action synonyms",
      "selection": "Keep E LAS/action for the mental clause and LAS/deeds for the bodily/verbal clause, each once.",
      "reason": "Both action and deeds in the second clause paraphrase its one LAS. Deeds is the selected occurrence with curated deed evidence, while action or remains an unbanked restatement. Preserve every distinct first/last compound and strict member; no borrowing the later transition term."
    },
    {
      "topic": "364 causal inference",
      "selection": "Keep E PAS NA/Thus d6; leave preceding YIN unbanked.",
      "reason": "PAS NA supplies the causal connection yielding the conclusion Thus; its actual glossary because and reference causal senses support the relation. The complete YIN PAS NA construction is a defensible broader phrase, but the prior copular predication is compressed and not exclusively owned by Thus. Whole YIN PAS NA has no HGM gloss. Retain uncertainty about YIN instead of an absence null."
    },
    {
      "topic": "365 source spelling and names",
      "selection": "Keep E complete author name, BRTSOMS PA/composed and entire book title.",
      "reason": "Current BRTZOMS converts to BRTSOMS and its complete PA entry explicitly lists composed/written. Other tense/vowel variants do not justify changing the printed source. The title and author name are attested; dates and introduction remain source wording without invented Tibetan counterparts."
    },
    {
      "topic": "365 named honorific",
      "selection": "Keep E RJE/Je and TSONG KHA PA/Tsongkapa d7.",
      "reason": "The full attested Je Tsongkapa name and independent Tsongkapa member identify Je locally as the remaining honorific in this proper name. RJE standalone glossary says lord, not Je, and pronunciation metadata alone would be insufficient. Preserve the T caution without misrepresenting the named-member evidence. MCHOG is separate and remains unbanked."
    },
    {
      "topic": "365 title members",
      "selection": "Keep E LAM/Path, RIM/Steps and CHEN MO/Great d7.",
      "reason": "The narrower members are complete words independently supported in this title. Actual LAM RIM/Steps of the Path and CHEN MO/Great Book attestations are genuine broader alternatives; they remain counterevidence. Book and title relations stay covered by the whole title without inventing a separate MO/book morpheme or moving MCHOG to Great."
    },
    {
      "topic": "366 topic and killing",
      "selection": "Add T NI/Here is as final p29; keep E SROG GCOD PA/killing.",
      "reason": "DANG PO NI introduces this first topic and the complete NI glossary explicitly supports here is, with no competing opening copula or demonstrative. Leave the article outside. Killing is a complete tighter realization of the full killing term, whose broader act of killing is also attested; do not invent life or a degenerate killing child."
    },
    {
      "topic": "366 Abbreviation and regrouping",
      "selection": "Keep E BSDU BAR/Abbreviation, BZHI BZHIR/into four d3 and both distinct BSDUS verbs.",
      "reason": "The inflected title is established by BSDU BA/Abbreviation and the citation verb. Preserve BAR. The complete repeated numeral expresses grouping into four; its components have reference support and the BZHIR mined gloss is labeled provisional. English fronts the total reduction and separately explains inclusion. Included and shortened belong to distinct source occurrences; later repeated four-part nouns cannot reuse the first-list words."
    },
    {
      "topic": "366 heads and negation",
      "selection": "Keep E BSHAD/presentation, BDE/easier, DGONGS PA/intention, ZHING/and, MI/in no way and GAL/violates.",
      "reason": "The nominal English recasting has identifiable local heads. DGONGS PA has actual glossary intention alongside curated thought; ZHING uses connective grammar rather than paradise. The whole negative English phrase belongs to MI and scopes over the separately identified violates. DANG relates that verb to intention and is not of the original text. Earlier material-intake caution requiring a whole MI GAL phrase was too broad; these complete adjacent exponents preserve the scope."
    },
    {
      "topic": "366 terminal closure",
      "selection": "Keep the E LO/null with its complete cls and nul explanation.",
      "reason": "LO closes the statement at the printed final period; its complete particle entry supports affirmative punctuation fusion. This does not justify nulling uncertain connectors, repeated source nouns or omitted framing."
    },
    {
      "topic": "364 source-role and register scope",
      "selection": "No errata; preserve E unresolved edition relationship and correct adopted T registered-class claim.",
      "reason": "The physical C05 transition and stars follow the completed explanation. C16 repeats the explanation with a different continuation; this supports a source-role inference, not an independently established identical registered defect or corrected edition. Keep the full original T claim and E question as provenance. Registry examples retain their actual scopes: E-071 running head, E-076/E-121 footnotes, E-120 omitted sickness. No source-specific correction is established."
    },
    {
      "topic": "All remaining omissions",
